      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just to clarify - I\u0027m ok with this CL _not_ working for CI builds. CI builds already have the right branch name information (I suppose it comes from the build scheduler). So my focus is to only get this information for developer builds.\n\n\n\u003e Maybe good enough, but I don\u0027t think this is always accurate, .repo/manifest.xml tells you which file in .repo/manifests/ is in use.\nAh right, yep. Getting this from the repo tool would be fantastic tbh.\n\n\u003e Maybe we should consider creating a new file that could be written out by a source tool with just this information that could be merged in?\n+1 to this as well! I just want to rule out the possibility that `repo` tool already doesn\u0027t write out this info somewhere. @jrn - any thoughts here?\n\n\u003e On the superproject side (including future use cases), we could add a static file to the superproject itself.\nSorry for the basic question - using `repo` tool is the default for Android developers currently - correct?\nAlso, can we just run git commands to get the branch / remote info for superproject?",
